            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0695" n="585" xml:id="pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5894: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-05T08:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                                1928—8 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:33
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>305. On August 7th Captain Edson, proceeding up Coco River with 46 marines,
                    attacked what believed to be the main body of outlaws about 20 miles below
                    Wamblan, inflicting known losses on the enemy of 10 killed, 3 wounded. One
                    marine named Meyer Stengel was killed and 3 wounded, the latter being now cared
                    for at Puerto Cabezas. Outlaws believed to be the retreating survivors of the
                    forces which engaged the American planes on July 25th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
